Here is a simple algorithm for checking if a number is prime:

  • Divide by 2 and continue if the quotient is less than or equal to zero;
  • Divide by the next prime number (3, 5, 7, ...) and continue if the quotient is less than or equal to zero;
  • If none of these has resulted in a quotient of zero, then the number is prime.

However, if the method involves checking a large number for divisibility by every prime number up to its square root, it will take a long time.

